# L1-OUT-003 / L2-WRT-021 (review finding M3): a SPURIOUS_DATA continuation
# stamped LATER than its errored parent, while the parent sits in an
# equal-timestamp run. The continuation opens the next run, so it follows
# whatever the parent's run ends with. Sorting that run would put the clean
# RT3 row last -- between the errored RT1 record and its continuation -- so
# the run is emitted in arrival order instead: RT3, RT1, continuation.

# RT3 SA11 Receive - clean @ .000500
0224 0F18 20DB F401 7E19 0004 0000 0000
2F00 22CA 2F00 22CA 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 71C7 0018

# RT1 SA11 Receive, ERRORED (Type Word bit 14) @ .000500
0248 0F18 20DB F401 7E09 0000 0000 1E01

# SPURIOUS_DATA continuation -> 0x2000, one microsecond later @ .000501
2005 0F18 20DB F501 0000
